Backport of local-inference-lab/b12x d7937d7fc2e5511a0b61eb3572cd149f563f9b4f
("feat(moe): prepare lossless FP4-CSF expert scales", Martin Vit, 2026-10-06; b12x
development now continues in flashinfer-ai/flashinfer, flashinfer/experimental/b12x):
only its producer-loop read-completion barrier ("Correct shared routing
synchronization"), verbatim. The producer loop's leader reuses the shared batch-claim
slot ctrl[7]; without the barrier after the read, a warp that is late to its read can
see the next claim. The same commit's deterministic shared-activation gather fix
(route_divisor in _w4a8_stage_a_tile_gather / _w4a8_stage_scale_tile_gather) is not
backported: those helpers serve the monolithic in-kernel FC1 path, which the ds41
specializations (external materialized FC1 / FC2) do not compile, and the external
phase-1 kernel already divides deterministic map entries by top-k with Int64 strides.
